window.CURRENT_TASK={"task_id": "L3-FUC-012-A3", "layer": "L3", "target_id": "FUC-012", "artifact_id": "FUC-012-A3", "title": "FUC-012 Exchange IFF and SIF Transponder Data / A3", "protocol_version": "L3_PURE_COVERAGE_3.0.0", "artifact_sha256": "19625a5e05bdeca5e3ca606f799b62c15ea23f323bcb71c927e0e6882cb37211", "source_sha256": "40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99", "reference_sha256": "b4f709b3589d863fab990eb4e08c03c115b5c04a0e0b03a147745c08ef83e087", "reference_origin": "agent_reference_reused", "instructions": "<pre>本包明确复用冻结的 Agent 来源参照，属于人工覆盖复评，不构成“真人独立建立参照”。不展示任何候选评分。FULL为全部实质含义覆盖；PARTIAL不折半分；NOT_COVERED未覆盖；CONTRADICTED矛盾；UNRESOLVED未决。来源未决统一保留在分母，不能猜成已确认；技术失败另列且留在分母。允许七槽联合表达。</pre>", "material_html": "<h3>Exchange IFF and SIF Transponder Data</h3><p>给定参与者：C2 JU</p><div class=\"source\"><p>许可来源：milstd6016b_sec4</p><a href=\"assets/40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">打开完整来源 PDF（含原页图像）</a> · <a href=\"assets/40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99.txt\" target=\"_blank\">同版全文文本</a></div><h3>冻结共同参照：已有 Agent 来源参照，非人工金标准</h3><pre>{&#x27;goal&#x27;: &#x27;Exchange IFF and SIF transponder data for surveillance tracks, including surveillance reporting, unique Mode II protection, clearing, difference resolution, update requests, and special code reporting applicable to a C2 JU&#x27;, &#x27;actor&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JU&#x27;, &#x27;start_boundary&#x27;: &#x27;When a C2 JU participates in Link 16 surveillance exchange and reports, receives, clears, requests, or resolves IFF/SIF modes and codes associated with surveillance tracks or points&#x27;, &#x27;success_boundary&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU reports IFF/SIF data when it has reporting responsibility, processes remote data and conflicts using the specified management messages and rules, and terminates or clears data only under the specified conditions&#x27;, &#x27;in_scope&#x27;: [&#x27;J3.2/J3.3 IFF/SIF surveillance data reporting by the JU with R2&#x27;, &#x27;J7.5 Clear IFF/SIF, Difference Report, Update Request, and Special Code messages&#x27;, &#x27;IFF/SIF difference resolution using Table 4.7-5&#x27;, &#x27;IFF/SIF reporting on J3.1 and J3.5 points where specified&#x27;, &#x27;Unique Mode II Code Protection&#x27;, &#x27;Current/noncurrent IFF/SIF data handling&#x27;, &#x27;Special code reporting&#x27;, &#x27;J3.XC1 transmission timing rules&#x27;], &#x27;out_of_scope&#x27;: [&#x27;General J3 track position, velocity, altitude, track quality, and reporting-responsibility rules not specific to IFF/SIF&#x27;, &#x27;PPLI own-unit periodic IFF/SIF reporting in J2 messages, except where received PPLI affects J3 reporting or J7.5 processing&#x27;, &#x27;Non-C2 JU data transmission&#x27;, &#x27;Track correlation procedures except IFF/SIF-specific Mode II protections&#x27;], &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 44, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The exchange of IFF/SIF modes and codes consists of five functional areas:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 45, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Each of the functional areas are described in the paragraphs indicated above.  The J2.XC1, J3.XC1, and J7.5 messages are used for this purpose as summarized in Table 4.4-6.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 118, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The J7.5 message with the following action values is used to perform this function:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 123, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;4.7.6.5  SPECIAL CODE REPORTING&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre><h3>交互目标 / goal</h3><pre>[goal:0 / CL-9cb98a740f5889ff] C2 JU aims to exchange IFF and SIF transponder data by transmitting available Modes I, II, and III Codes in J3.1/J3.5 (PTI = 0) messages and reporting IFF/SIF surveillance data in J3.2C1/J3.3C1 words for Air and Surface tracks.</pre><h3>前置条件 / preconditions</h3><pre>[preconditions:0 / CL-17fcd3d598974be9] IFF/SIF transponder data, including Modes I, II, and III Codes when available, is available for exchange.</pre><pre>[preconditions:1 / CL-85da4e96f1da6c02] C2 JU has correlated local sensor data and holds R² for the tracks whose IFF/SIF surveillance data it reports in J3.2C1/J3.3C1 words.</pre><pre>[preconditions:2 / CL-85a2087ebee85825] C2 JU is in Active status and has completed sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration after initially achieving Active status or returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure before transmitting the affected tracks.</pre><h3>触发条件 / trigger</h3><pre>[trigger:0 / CL-38bcb8c679cfb25b] The use case is triggered when locally entered IFF/SIF data changes from zero to nonzero or from one nonzero value to another.</pre><h3>主流程 / main_flow</h3><pre>[main_flow:0 / CL-3bdb368fbeda94fe / step 1] C2 JU selects the IFF/SIF data to report for the track; if locally derived IFF/SIF data differs from the data being reported in the PPLI message, C2 JU reports the locally derived data.</pre><pre>[main_flow:1 / CL-680597ddbfeb513f / step 2] C2 JU with R² exchanges IFF/SIF modes and codes by reporting all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for the track in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages.</pre><pre>[main_flow:2 / CL-601db11691386beb / step 3] C2 JU transmits IFF/SIF surveillance data (J3.XC1) at the next opportunity for new tracks when assuming R² or when data changes, periodically at 1/8 the basic message rate for realtime tracks, and with each NRT track report.</pre><pre>[main_flow:3 / CL-702096e4b112a93d / step 4] C2 JU selects the applicable IFF/SIF surveillance message for the track category: J3.2 for Air tracks or J3.3 for Surface (Maritime) tracks.</pre><pre>[main_flow:4 / CL-19212ef2b0801253 / step 5] When C2 JU receives remote Mode I or III data and has no own unit data (R² UNIT NO DATA), C2 JU accepts the data and transmits it in a J3.XC1 word at the next transmit opportunity (AT).</pre><pre>[main_flow:5 / CL-d49348163176f033 / step 6] C2 JU sets the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator in the J3 message to value 2 when all IFF/SIF nonzero mode codes were obtained from or are the same as the codes received in the J2 message for the subject TN; otherwise, if the Mode II code was obtained from or is the same as the Mode II code received in the J2 message, C2 JU sets the indicator to value 1.</pre><pre>[main_flow:6 / CL-b8a1dec61a3bf726 / step 7] Software inhibits any change to a valid Mode II code for the specific local track.</pre><pre>[main_flow:7 / CL-0998bf3c788b2e73 / step 8] C2 JU treats all unique Mode II codes as unique tracks.</pre><pre>[main_flow:8 / CL-1be0caa8e6347f2a / step 9] When local sensors detect a Mode II code change, C2 JU treats it as a new track.</pre><pre>[main_flow:9 / CL-dfd1aba1322a00f4 / step 10] Receiving units that hold valid nonzero IFF/SIF data respond as required by the IFF/SIF Difference Resolution Matrix, Table 4.7-5.</pre><h3>备选流程 / alternative_flow</h3><pre>[alternative_flow:0 / CL-d0a9ff01ea05b902 / step 1] Diverges from Step 2: when locally entered IFF/SIF data changes from zero to a nonzero value or from one nonzero value to another, C2 JU reports the difference in accordance with Table 4.7-5 IFF/SIF Difference Resolution Matrix, using a J7.5 (ACT = 1) message to transmit the IFF/SIF Difference Report.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:1 / CL-a0639856c8396b32 / step 2] Diverges from Step 3: in response to operator action, a JU transmits a J7.5 (ACT = 2) IFF/SIF Update Request to initiate data updating, providing a manual alternative to the periodic or event-driven surveillance transmission.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:2 / CL-ec4c16e284fa0f10 / step 3] Diverges from Step 3: data updating can occur spontaneously when the R² unit reports a No Data status (value 0) for one or more modes in a required IFF/SIF Surveillance data report, J3.XC1.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:3 / CL-9d3bf3019696bb5b / step 4] Diverges from Step 4: if the locally held Environment/Category of a track differs from the Environment/Category received in a J3.X or J7.0 (ACT = 1) message for that track, the operator is alerted, even when the received Environment/Category is not implemented.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:4 / CL-0d910447371f841b / step 5] Diverges from Step 4: when a JU changes the Environment/Category of a track (e.g., Space to air, Air to space/surface/land), or when an operator rejects a difference report, and the JU has R², C2 JU transmits the local Environment/Category in the appropriate Surveillance report.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:5 / CL-e1ae08523c5cc19b / step 6] Diverges from Step 10: when a controlling unit receives a J7.0 (ACT = 1) message reporting an ID different from local ID data, it automatically rejects the received ID and originates a J7.0 (ACT = 1) message containing the local ID data with the Controlling Unit Indicator field set to value 1.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:6 / CL-dc50986a579c736e / step 7] Diverges from Step 10: for NonR² JUs, when an ID conflict is indicated, the unit may take no action with respect to the reported ID; in this variant, an operator alert may be provided as a system option.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:7 / CL-59ef0cec5a9ca144 / step 8] Diverges from Step 10: in the case of ID conflicts, the differences are presented to the operators for their evaluation, and these conflicts may also require voice coordination for final resolution.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:8 / CL-cd9a62c82e39b5de / step 9] Diverges from Step 10: when a NonR² unit receives a J7.5 (ACT = 2) message from the R² unit and holds valid local data (nonzero codes) for the requested mode(s), it responds by initiating a J7.5 (ACT = 1) message; if the requested data has already been transmitted by another JU, the remaining JUs need not respond with their local data.</pre><h3>异常流程 / exception_flow</h3><pre>[exception_flow:0 / CL-4229dc18d18519a5 / step 2] Diverges from Step 2 when an IFF/SIF Mode I, II, or III code field is all zeroes: an all-zero code is illegal for use as an assigned operational IFF/SIF Mode I, II, or III code and indicates that the reporting unit has no data; the branch treats that code field as indicating no data.</pre><pre>[exception_flow:1 / CL-bd762fe001d5e4d1 / step 3] Diverges from Step 3 when a JU with R² receives or initiates a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message that results in no IFF/SIF data being held on the track: the JU shall not continue transmitting the periodic J3 message containing the continuation word with IFF/SIF data; the branch inhibits that continuing transmission.</pre><pre>[exception_flow:2 / CL-c771f3f8eeea811b / step 10] Diverges from Step 10 when an IFF/SIF data conflict alert occurs during difference resolution: the operator has manual resolution actions available, including updating local data, initiating clear messages, initiating difference reports, changing local data to agree with remote, or decorrelating local data to assign a new track number.</pre><pre>[exception_flow:3 / CL-aa0f047df2702078 / step 10] Diverges from Step 10 when the same report is transmitted twice within 30 seconds during difference resolution: automatic transmission of the J7.5 (ACT = 1) message is inhibited and the operator is alerted (TC condition).</pre><h3>后置条件 / postconditions</h3><pre>[postconditions:0 / CL-54b8c897e84287ec] IFF/SIF transponder data is exchanged through the specified J-series messages.</pre><pre>[postconditions:1 / CL-a9131c2e1be2ed30] Following successful IFF/SIF difference resolution, the system state reflects the applicable resolution outcome: the local unit accepts and transmits received data in a J3.XC1 word (AT), accepts and transmits J3.XC1 on upgrade or rejects on downgrade with operator alert (AC1), accepts data on upgrade or takes no action on downgrade (AC2), accepts data on upgrade or rejects and transmits local data via J7.5 (ACT=1) on downgrade (AC3), or simply accepts the data (A).</pre>", "groups": [{"key": "coverage", "title": "逐需求覆盖", "fields": [{"key": "label", "label": "覆盖标签", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["FULL", "PARTIAL", "NOT_COVERED", "CONTRADICTED", "UNRESOLVED", "TECHNICAL_FAILURE"]}, {"key": "location", "label": "输出位置/断言 ID/原文；无匹配填无", "type": "textarea", "required": true}, {"key": "reason", "label": "判定理由（列出遗漏的条件、否定、顺序或结果）", "type": "textarea", "required": true}], "rows": [{"title": "S16-06-R0001", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU participating in the exchange of IFF/SIF modes and codes shall support the five functional areas: IFF/SIF Surveillance Data Reporting, Unique Mode II Code Protection, Clearing IFF/SIF Data, IFF/SIF Difference Resolution, and IFF/SIF Update Request.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 44, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The exchange of IFF/SIF modes and codes consists of five functional areas:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 44, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;a.  IFF/SIF Surveillance Data Reporting (this paragraph). \\n \\n \\nb.  Unique Mode II Code Protection (paragraph 4.7.6.1).&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0002", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When reporting IFF/SIF surveillance data for Air tracks, the C2 JU with R2 shall report the data in the J3.2C1 word; when reporting for Surface tracks, it shall report the data in the J3.3C1 word.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The reporting of IFF/SIF surveillance data in the J3.2C1 and J3.3C1 words for Air and Surface tracks, respectively, is the responsibility of the JU with R2&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0003", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU with R2 shall report all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for a track in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages, including codes from own sensors, manually entered codes, or codes accepted under Table 4.7-5.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;R2 units shall report all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that track in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Valid code responses are those codes which have been received from own sensors on two or more successive interrogations for Modes I, II, and III with the same value, one interrogation for Mode IV, manually entered codes, or codes accepted in accordance with the IFF/SIF Difference Resolution Matrix, Table 4.7-5.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0004", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When no valid code is held for a subject local or remote track/mode, the C2 JU shall report the No Data condition as zeroes in the applicable Mode Code field of the J3 continuation word.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;No Data:  No valid code is currently held for the subject local or remote track/mode.  (This condition is reported as zeroes in the applicable Mode Code field of the J3 continuation word.)&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0005", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall treat received code responses as Valid Data when they are received from own sensors on two or more successive interrogations with the same value for Modes I, II, and III, after one interrogation for Mode IV, when manually entered, or when accepted under Table 4.7-5; it shall report Valid Data by entering the nonzero code in the applicable Mode Code field of the J3 continuation word.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Valid Data:  Valid code responses are those codes which have been received from own sensors on two or more successive interrogations for Modes I, II, and III with the same value, one interrogation for Mode IV, manually entered codes, or codes accepted in accordance with the IFF/SIF Difference Resolution Matrix, Table 4.7-5.  This condition will be reported by entering the nonzero code in the applicable Mode Code field of the J3 continuation word.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0006", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When IFF/SIF code values change from No Data to Valid Data or from Valid Data to other Valid Data, the C2 JU shall report the change.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any change in the IFF/SIF code values from a No Data status to Valid Data or changes from Valid Data to other Valid Data will be reported as occurring.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0007", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A change from Valid Data to No Data resulting from the J7.5 (ACT = 0) clearing function shall not cause transmission of a change report.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Changes from a Valid Data value to a No Data status as a result of the clearing function (J7.5 (ACT = 0)) will not cause the transmission of a change report.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0008", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall consider changes derived from both local and remote sources for IFF/SIF reporting.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Changes derived from both local and remote sources shall be considered for reporting in accordance with this rule.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0009", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A track with Valid Data that subsequently fails to respond to interrogations shall not be changed to No Data unless a Clear action is taken.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 47, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Tracks with Valid Data which subsequently fail to respond to interrogations shall not be changed to the No Data status unless a Clear action is taken.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0010", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When available, the C2 JU shall transmit IFF/SIF Modes I, II, and III codes in the J3.1 and J3.5 (PTI = 0) messages.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 20, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;IFF/SIF data (Modes I, II, and III Codes) are transmitted in the J3.1 and J3.5 (PTI = 0) messages when available.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0011", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The IFF/SIF data in a J3.1 message shall contain the IFF/SIF modes and codes of the previously reported track for which the emergency point was initiated.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 20, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The IFF/SIF data in the J3.1 message shall contain the IFF/SIF modes and codes of the previously reported track for which the emergency point was initiated.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0012", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU that assumes R2 of an inactive or limited-status interface unit and reports it as a track or point shall report the most current IFF/SIF data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 9, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The most current IFF/SIF data shall be reported.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0013", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When all nonzero IFF/SIF mode codes for an assumed-R2 interface unit were obtained from, or are the same as, codes received in the J2 message for the subject TN, the C2 JU shall report the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator in the J3 message as value 2.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 9, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If all IFF/SIF nonzero mode codes were obtained from or are the same as the codes received in the J2 message for the subject TN, the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator in the J3 message shall be reported as value 2.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0014", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If not all nonzero IFF/SIF mode codes match the J2 message but the Mode II code was obtained from, or is the same as, the Mode II code received in the J2 message, the C2 JU shall report the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator as value 1.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 9, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Otherwise, if the Mode II code was obtained from or is the same as the Mode II code received in the J2 message, the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator shall be reported as value 1.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0015", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If neither the all-codes condition nor the Mode II condition applies, the C2 JU shall report the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator as value 0.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 9, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Otherwise, the PPLI IFF/SIF Indicator shall be reported as value 0.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0016", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The Mode IV Indicator value reported by the C2 JU shall be based on actual responses received and shall not be based solely on the TN having previously been received in a PPLI message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 9, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The Mode IV Indicator value reported shall be based on actual responses received and shall not be based on the fact that the TN was previously received in a PPLI message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0017", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If locally derived IFF/SIF data differs from IFF/SIF data reported in the PPLI message, the C2 JU shall report the locally derived data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 9, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If locally derived IFF/SIF data differs from IFF/SIF data that was being reported in the PPLI message, the locally derived data shall be reported.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0018", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall use J7.5 action 0 for Clear IFF/SIF, action 1 for IFF/SIF Difference Report, action 2 for IFF/SIF Update Request, and action 3 for Special Code.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 118, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;a.  J7.5 (ACT = 0) Clear IFF/SIF message. \\n \\n \\nb.  J7.5 (ACT = 1) IFF/SIF Difference Report message. \\n \\n \\nc.  J7.5 (ACT = 2) IFF/SIF Update Request message. \\n \\n \\nd.  J7.5 (ACT = 3) Special Code message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0019", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A code consisting of all zeroes is illegal for use as an assigned operational IFF/SIF Mode I, II, or III code; an all-zero Mode I, II, or III Code field indicates that the reporting unit has No Data for that mode.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 118, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;A code of all zeroes (00 or 0000) is illegal for use as an assigned operational IFF/SIF Mode I, II, or III code.  Any IFF/SIF Mode I, II, or III Code field set to all zeroes indicates that the reporting unit has no data&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0020", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Software shall inhibit any change to a valid Mode II code for a specific local track.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 119, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Software shall inhibit any change to a valid Mode II code for the specific local track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0021", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Initiation or receipt of a J7.5 (ACT = 0) Clear IFF/SIF message designating all modes or the Mode II code of a specified track shall cause the Mode II code status to return to No Data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 119, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;However, the initiation or receipt of the J7.5 (ACT = 0) Clear IFF/SIF message, designating all modes or Mode II code of the specified track to be cleared, shall cause the Mode II code status to be returned to a No Data status.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0022", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When local sensors detect a Mode II code change, the C2 JU shall treat it as a new track.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 119, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When local sensors detect a Mode II code change, it shall be treated as a new track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0023", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU may alert operators when two or more tracks have the same Mode II code.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 119, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Operators may be alerted when two or more tracks have the same Mode II code.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0024", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;All unique Mode II codes should be treated as unique tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 119, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;All unique Mode II codes should be treated as unique tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0025", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU capable of originating a J3 message that includes a continuation word containing IFF/SIF data shall also have a capability to manually originate a J7.5 (ACT = 0) Clear IFF/SIF message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 119, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Accordingly, any JU capable of originating a J3 message that includes a continuation word containing IFF/SIF data shall also have a capability to manually originate the J7.5 (ACT = 0) message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0026", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU capable of maintaining IFF/SIF data in its database shall, upon initiation or receipt of a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message, have a capability to automatically set the designated mode or modes for the specified track to No Data, subject to the Mode IV exception.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 119, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Additionally, any JU capable of maintaining IFF/SIF data in its database shall have a capability, upon initiation or receipt of a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message, to automatically set the designated mode(s) for the specified track&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0027", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU may originate a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message for clearing one or more modes on a specified track only by operator action.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 120, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any JU may originate, by operator action only, the J7.5 (ACT = 0) message for the clearing of one or more modes on the specified track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0028", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Upon receipt of a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message, the C2 JU shall automatically set the designated mode or modes for the specified track to No Data, except that acceptance or rejection of a received Mode IV Clear message may be automatic or by operator determination.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 120, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;All JUs, upon receipt of the J7.5 (ACT = 0) message, shall automatically set the designated mode(s) for the specified track to the No Data status (except that acceptance or rejection of a received J7.5 (ACT=0) Mode IV Clear message may be automatic or by operator determination).&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0029", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If No Data is accepted after a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message, the C2 JU should use the No Data status for subsequent interface functions and data link messages until updated by valid local or remote code responses, and the operator display shall indicate that the clear message was received.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 120, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The No Data status, if accepted, should be used for all subsequent interface functions and data link messages until updated by valid code responses from local or remote sources.  The operator display shall indicate that a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message was received.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0030", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If a C2 JU with R2 receives or initiates a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message that results in no IFF/SIF data being held on the track, it shall not continue transmitting the periodic J3 message that includes the continuation word containing IFF/SIF data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 120, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;A JU with R2, upon receiving or initiating a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message that results in no IFF/SIF data being held on the track, shall not continue transmitting the periodic J3 message that includes the continuation word containing IFF/SIF data.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0031", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU may change a local mode to No Data without transmitting a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 120, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any JU may change a local mode to a No Data status without transmitting a J7.5 (ACT = 0) message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0032", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU without R2 shall compare locally held IFF/SIF data with data reported by the JU with R2 and shall report current valid changes.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 120, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Each JU without R2 shall compare locally held data with IFF/SIF data reported by the JU with R2 and report any valid data that are different, in accordance with the rules below.  The JU without R2 shall report current valid changes.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0033", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU receiving a J3 message containing remote IFF/SIF data or a J7.5 (ACT = 1) message differing from locally held data shall respond as indicated in Table 4.7-5.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 120, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any JU receiving a J3 message that includes a continuation word with remote IFF/SIF data or J7.5 (ACT = 1) message differing from locally held data shall respond as indicated in Table 4.7-5.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0034", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When a C2 JU without R2 enters a nonzero-to-nonzero or zero-to-nonzero change in locally held Mode I, III, or IV data, or a zero-to-nonzero change in Mode II data, it shall automatically report the new data in a J7.5 (ACT = 1) message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 122, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any JU without R2 entering a change of nonzero to nonzero or zero to nonzero value to its locally held Mode I, III or IV IFF/SIF data, or a change from zero to nonzero Mode II data, shall automatically report the new data in a J7.5 (ACT = 1) message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0035", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When an operator receives an IFF/SIF data conflict alert required by Table 4.7-5, the C2 JU shall make the specified manual resolution actions available.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 122, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When an operator receives an IFF/SIF data conflict alert as required in Table 4.7-5, he shall have the following manual actions at his disposal for attempting resolution of the difference:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0036", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Current IFF/SIF data are valid code responses no more than 40 seconds old since entry into the database by automatic or manual inputs; the C2 JU is not required to time-tag IFF/SIF data solely to determine currency.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 122, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Current IFF/SIF data, as defined for use in Table 4.7-5, are those valid code responses that are no more than 40 seconds old since entry into the database by automatic or manual inputs.  However, systems need not time-tag IFF/SIF data for purposes of determining currency.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0037", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When remote IFF/SIF data is accepted under Table 4.7-5, the C2 JU shall enter it as valid noncurrent data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 122, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When remote IFF/SIF data is accepted in accordance with the difference resolution matrix, Table 4.7-5, such remote data will be entered as valid noncurrent data.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0038", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If a C2 JU does not maintain currency indicators, it shall assume a local track/mode is current when it is currently being received automatically from own sensors; all other code data shall be assumed noncurrent, except Mode IV processing is exempt from current/noncurrent indications.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 122, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Systems not maintaining currency indicators will assume local track/mode is current if the track/mode is currently being received automatically from own sensors.  All other code data shall be assumed to be noncurrent.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 123, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Processing of Mode IV codes is exempt from all current/noncurrent indications.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0039", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A J7.5 (ACT = 2) IFF/SIF Update Request shall be manually initiated by R2 and nonR2 units, with the applicable mode indicators set when requesting update of IFF/SIF data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 123, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The J7.5 (ACT = 2) message shall be manually initiated by R2 and nonR2 units with the applicable mode indicators set when requesting update of IFF/SIF data.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0040", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU with R2 receiving a J7.5 (ACT = 2) message shall respond by initiating a J3.XC1 message regardless of No Data status.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 123, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;R2 units receiving the J7.5 (ACT = 2) message will respond by initiating a J3.XC1 message regardless of the No Data status.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0041", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A nonR2 C2 JU receiving a J7.5 (ACT = 2) message from the R2 unit shall respond by initiating J7.5 (ACT = 1) if valid nonzero local data are held for the requested mode or modes; if another JU has transmitted the requested data, remaining JUs need not respond.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 123, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;NonR2 units receiving the J7.5 (ACT = 2) message from the R2 unit will respond by initiating a J7.5 (ACT = 1) message if valid local data (nonzero codes) are held for the requested mode(s).  If the requested data has been transmitted by another JU, the remaining JUs need not respond with their local data.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0042", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU without R2 shall not respond to a J7.5 (ACT = 2) update request received from another nonR2 unit.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 123, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;NonR2 units receiving the J7.5 (ACT = 2) message from other nonR2 units will not respond to the request.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0043", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU implementing special codes shall provide nonambiguous displays for IFF/SIF code responses and special code responses, and when more than one special-code field is implemented it shall clearly distinguish each type of special code from all other types.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;JUs implementing the special codes capability shall provide nonambiguous displays for both IFF/SIF code responses and the special code responses.  Also, JUs implementing more than one of the special code fields shall provide nonambiguous displays which clearly distinguish each type of special code from all other types of special codes.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0044", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The rules for reporting and managing J7.5 (ACT = 3) shall govern special codes, and the general IFF/SIF data rules shall not govern them.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The rules for reporting and managing the J7.5 (ACT = 3) message shall be as stated in this paragraph and are not governed by the rules for IFF/SIF data.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0045", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU may use J7.5 (ACT = 3) to initiate, change, or clear special codes.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any JU may report special codes using the J7.5 (ACT = 3) message to initiate, change, or clear such codes.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0046", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When clearing one or more special codes, the C2 JU shall transmit J7.5 (ACT = 3) with the special-code applicability indicator fields set and the associated special-code fields set to zero.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any JU clearing one or more of the special codes shall transmit the J7.5 (ACT = 3) message with the special code applicability indicator fields set and the associated special code fields set to value 0.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0047", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU implementing the special-code capability shall accept all zero or nonzero special-code values as received.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;JUs implementing the special code capability shall accept all zero or nonzero special code values as received.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0048", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall transmit special-code information only if data are held.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;A JU shall transmit special code information only if data are held.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0049", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU originating or changing a special code shall assume J7.5 (ACT = 3) reporting responsibility for retransmission until a special-code message is received from another unit, the track is dropped, or a clear special code is received.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The JU originating or changing a special code shall assume J7.5 (ACT = 3) reporting responsibility for retransmission until such time as a special code message is received for that track from another unit, or the track is dropped, or a clear special code is received.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0050", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When a C2 JU has or assumes reporting responsibility for the track surveillance report and implements J7.5 (ACT = 3), it shall also have reporting responsibility for nonzero special codes.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The JU having or assuming reporting responsibility for the track surveillance report shall also have reporting responsibility for nonzero special codes if that system implements the J7.5 (ACT = 3) message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0051", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When a C2 JU transmits a J7.5 (ACT = 3) Special Code message, it shall report all nonzero special codes for that track.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 124, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When a JU transmits a J7.5 (ACT = 3) Special Code message all nonzero special codes for that track will be reported.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0052", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall transmit J3.XC1 words periodically at 1/8 the basic message rate for realtime tracks and with each NRT track report.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 46, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;PERIODICALLY - AT 1/8 THE \\n  BASIC MESSAGE RATE FOR \\n  REALTIME TRACKS AND \\n  WITH EACH NRT TRACK \\n  REPORT&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0053", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall transmit J3.XC1 words at the next opportunity for new tracks when assuming R2 or when data change.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 46, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;TRANSMITTED AT NEXT \\n  OPPORTUNITY FOR NEW \\n  TRACKS WHEN ASSUMING R2 \\n  OR WHEN DATA CHANGE.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0054", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall transmit J3.XC1 words at the next opportunity after accepting or rejecting remote data received in J7.5 (ACT = 1) message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 46, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;TRANSMITTED AT NEXT \\n  OPPORTUNITY AFTER \\n  ACCEPTING OR REJECTING \\n  REMOTE DATA RECEIVED \\n  IN J7.5 (ACT = 1) \\n  MESSAGE.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0055", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall transmit J3.XC1 words at the next opportunity in response to J7.1 (ACT = 1) Data Update Request and to a J7.5 (ACT = 2) IFF/SIF Update Request.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 46, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;TRANSMITTED AT NEXT \\n  OPPORTUNITY IN \\n  RESPONSE TO J7.1 \\n  (ACT = 1) DATA \\n  UPDATE REQUEST AND \\n  TO A J7.5 (ACT = 2) \\n  IFF/SIF UPDATE \\n  REQUEST.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-06-R0056", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If the same J7.5 (ACT=1) report is transmitted twice within 30 seconds, automatic transmission of the J7.5 (ACT=1) message is inhibited and the operator is alerted (TC condition in Table 4.7-5).&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 121, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;TC = TRANSMIT LOCAL DATA IN A J7.5 (ACT = 1) MESSAGE. IF THE SAME REPORT IS TRANSMITTED TWICE WITHIN 30 SECONDS, AUTOMATIC TRANSMISSION OF THE J7.5 ACT = 1) MESSAGE IS INHIBITED AND THE OPERATOR IS ALERTED.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;Legend of Table 4.7-5&#x27;}]}</pre>"}], "repeat": false, "min_rows": 0}], "blockers": [], "requirement_meta": [{"id": "S16-06-R0001", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0002", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0003", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0004", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0005", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0006", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0007", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0008", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0009", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0010", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0011", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0012", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0013", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0014", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0015", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0016", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0017", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0018", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0019", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0020", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0021", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0022", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0023", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0024", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0025", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0026", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0027", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0028", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0029", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0030", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0031", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0032", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0033", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0034", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0035", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0036", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0037", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0038", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0039", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0040", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0041", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0042", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0043", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0044", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0045", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0046", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0047", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0048", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0049", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0050", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0051", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0052", "status": "REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0053", "status": "REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0054", "status": "REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0055", "status": "REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED"}, {"id": "S16-06-R0056", "status": "REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED"}], "no_content": false, "material_sha256": "b1a7c4e253c7378a9b888d0bf62e8b1550538c6cb56e314bd8dbf799bf3479d1"};
